# Every checkout keeps repository text as LF, whatever the local Git line-ending
# setting is (Git for Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true). Scripts, tests,
# hashes and tooling in this tree read exact LF bytes; a CRLF checkout breaks
# them. Git still auto-detects binary content; text it detects is LF on disk.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Preserve the approved application-icon master byte-for-byte on every checkout.
packages/app/icon-source/cbe-toolbox-icon.svg -text

# Committed binary formats stay byte-opaque, independent of content detection.
# Only formats the tree actually tracks are listed here.
*.png -text
*.jpg -text
*.ico -text
*.icns -text
*.woff2 -text
*.zip -text
*.pdf -text
*.docx -text
*.xlsx -text
